/* ============================================================
   Trap Dungeons 2 - levels.js
   Data-driven level definitions. Each room is a 15x10 ASCII
   map plus a declarative list of traps. Compare with v1 where
   every level was a Phaser scene full of nested skip-conditions:
   here adding a room means adding data, not code.

   Map legend
     #  solid brick            =  half brick (solid)
     .  empty                  ~  FAKE brick (looks solid, isn't)
     c  crumble brick          ^  spikes pointing up (deadly)
     v  spikes hanging down    x  FAKE spikes (look deadly, aren't)
     s  spring                 S  mega spring
     h  heart pickup           P  player spawn
     D  exit door

   Trap triggers use tile units ({x,y,w,h} rectangles).
   All twelve rooms are original layouts built on the classic
   trap-platformer vocabulary: pop-up spikes, crumbling floors,
   lying doors, ghost blocks, crushers and one final gag.
   ============================================================ */
